P00063-Fasta_Statistic	Sequence Analyses	Xiao Chen	chenxiao.email@qq.com	This script is used to analyze nucleotide or amino acid sequence files.\n 1. During analysis, any '*' characters in the sequences are removed. The script performs case-insensitive matching for GAP(N), ATCG, and amino acid sequences.\n 2.The statistics generated include the number of sequences in the file, N50, the total length, GC content, and GAP(N) content of each sequence and the entire set of sequences. \n 3.For amino acid sequences, GAP and GC content can be ignored. \n 4.For nucleotide sequences, calculations such as the length of a single sequence, total sequence length, N50 length, average length, and the lengths of the longest and shortest sequences include GAP(N). However, GC content for a single sequence and the overall nucleotide sequence GC content are calculated as the proportion of GC bases to the total ATCG bases (excluding GAP).	https://share.feijipan.com/s/qVVIsSoC
P00064-splitSuperBigGenome	Sequence Analyses	Zhougeng Xu	xuzhougeng@163.com	A plugin for splitting large chromosomes in big genomes and processing corresponding GTF files. When a chromosome exceeds 512mb in length, some bioinformatics tools start to malfunction. Considering current large genomes are unlikely to be completed as a single piece and are typically connected through scaffolding methods linking multiple contigs, this tool was developed for splitting purposes.	https://share.feijipan.com/s/dGVItTAW
